Relevant columns and their possible roles  

bigquery-public-data.noaa_gsod.stations  
• usaf           : station id –‑ join key to daily file  
• wban           : station id –‑ 2nd part of join key  
• name           : search for “ROCHESTER” stations  
• country        : keep US stations (country = 'US')  
• state          : decide which Rochester (NY = “NY”, MN = “MN”, etc.)  
• lat / lon      : geographical check if several stations match  
• begin / end    : be sure the station was active in 2019  

bigquery-public-data.noaa_gsod.gsod2019  
• stn / wban     : join to “usaf / wban” in stations  
• year / mo / da : build the date field  
• temp           : mean daily air temperature (°F) → convert to °C  
• prcp           : daily precipitation (inch) → convert to cm  
• wdsp           : mean wind speed (knots, stored as string) → convert to m s‑¹  
• any “9999.9 / 999.9 / 999.9” : missing value flags –‑ filter out or turn into NULL  

Typical filters / conditions that will be used  
• LOWER(name) LIKE '%rochester%'  
• country = 'US'  
• CONCAT(year,'-',mo,'-',da) BETWEEN '2019-01-01' AND '2019-03-31'  
• temp  <> 9999.9, prcp <> 99.99, CAST(wdsp AS FLOAT64) <> 999.9  

